HARMONIC ARITHMETIC for monopole (l=0) propagating modes
  a mode of co-rotating frequency Omega emits into the matter band
  through its n-th harmonic when n*Omega >= Omega_c = m - w.
  The lowest crossing n is the leading radiative order; n = 1 means
  the mode radiates directly (a golden-rule width linear in the
  density of states), n >= 2 means direct emission is BLOCKED and the
  leading channel is n-quantum -- which is exactly the regime where
  HC-4's 'width proportional to amplitude^2' pre-registration does NOT
  apply unmodified.

  CAVEAT (review Finding 7) -- the Omega values in this table are
  SINGLE-OPERATOR ESTIMATES, Omega(lambda) = sqrt(w^2+lambda) - w applied
  to eigenvalues of L0 / Lx_sym / Lx_flav separately. The true BdG
  frequencies of the coupled (x,y) system come from the quadratic pencil,
  which HC-1 solves ONLY for the l=0 symmetric sector and only there with
  a box-convergence test. Where the two disagree the COUPLED, box-tested
  result in hc1_bound_modes.tsv is authoritative: e.g. at w=1.32 the
  single-operator L0 spectrum shows six sub-threshold entries, while the
  box-converged coupled solve (Rmax = 5 r_rms = 113) shows ZERO bound
  internal modes -- the apparent ladder was a box artifact of an
  undersized domain. Treat this table as a CLASSIFICATION of candidate
  modes by channel, not as a measured frequency list.
